// #1074 PR review (chatgpt-codex-connector, P1): "Respect local shadowing
// when forwarding evidence". evidence_dict_pass's needing-forwarding
// rewrite (edp_rewrite_needing_body, inline_direct_perform.vibe) matches a
// call's callee by NAME ONLY against the globally-collected `needing` set
// (top-level functions that need the evidence dict threaded to them), with
// no scope tracking. Here `via`'s own body locally binds a NEW `helper`
// (pure, ignoring effects entirely) that shadows the TOP-LEVEL effectful
// `helper` -- before the #1074 fix, `via`'s `helper()` call (correctly
// resolving to the LOCAL, pure helper by ordinary lexical scoping) still
// got the evidence-dict argument incorrectly prepended, since the local
// closure was never rewritten to accept that extra parameter -- producing
// "null function or function signature mismatch" at runtime.
//
// History: #1074 fixed this by dropping a shadowed needing name entirely
// (edp_drop_shadowed_needing), which parked this program on the replay
// frontier -- this fixture was the last remaining genuine replay
// execution. ADR-0076 追記34 V2 removed replay, so the shadowing binder
// is now α-renamed instead (edp_alpha_rename_shadowed, fresh
// `__edpsh_N_helper`): the name-only match becomes exact, `helper`
// migrates like any other needing function, and the local call still
// resolves to the (renamed) pure closure. The value is unchanged; what
// this fixture pins flipped from "shadowing suppresses migration safely"
// to "shadowing no longer suppresses migration at all".
//   via() => local pure helper, ignores its own perform-free body, => 42
//   helper() (outer, top-level) => perform Ask::Get resolves to 5 => 5
//   total: 42 + 5 = 47
effect Ask {
  Get -> Int
}

let helper = () -> Int with Ask {
  perform Ask::Get
}

let via = () -> Int with Ask {
  let helper = () -> Int { 42 }
  helper()
}

export let main = () -> Int {
  handle {
    via() + helper()
  } with Ask {
    Get => resume(5)
  }
}

// #1571: the expectation lives here, checked by `inspect` and updatable
// with `vibe test --update`, instead of in a `__DATA__` tail the gate has
// to `sed` off and compare in shell.
test "evidence dict needing shadowed by local" {
  inspect(main(), "47")
}
